				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "CAN activity indicator, hardware-driven from the TCAN1042 RXD line - no GPIO and no software. RXD idles high (recessive) and pulls low on dominant, so the LED lights on bus traffic. USE A RED LED: its ~1.9-2.0V forward drop leaves headroom on 3.3V, where green or blue at 2.8-3.2V would barely conduct. EXPECTED BEHAVIOUR - a dim STEADY glow when traffic is present and dark when the bus is silent; it is modulated by dominant duty cycle (~30%) so it never blinks visibly and will look faint. That is correct, not a fault. Diagnostic value: lit means frames are reaching the transceiver, which separates 'the bus is dead' from 'the software is not reading it' - a distinction SSH cannot give you because it is upstream of software."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
