		(property "Description" "CAN FD transceiver with VIO level shifting, SOIC-8"
			(at 143.51 59.69 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "CAN transceiver. STB (pin 8) MOVED FROM GND TO GPIO22 IN REV 2.0 - this is a behaviour change with a software prerequisite. The pin has an INTERNAL PULL-UP forcing standby when it floats, and a Pi GPIO is high-Z at boot, so the board comes up with the transceiver in standby and can0 receives NOTHING - link up, no errors, no frames. Something must drive STB low on every boot. Prefer a gpio-hog in the board overlay over the daemon: it asserts before userspace exists and survives a crash. Low-power-by-default is the DESIRED behaviour (S13.3.1 depends on it), so this is a driver requirement, not a pin to re-tie. RXD also drives D6's activity LED (~1.2 mA) - within its +/-2 mA spec, with margin against the MCP2518FD's Vil."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
